{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 2: epic 061c plan-review returned BLOCK (blocking=6 advisory=16). Ran the out-of-loop capability spike the coaching asked for, against pinned pydantic-ai 1.107.1 in the worktree venv. RESULTS — all 'UNRESOLVED' advisories were static-resolution false alarms: (1) infer_model(model, provider_factory: Callable[[str], Provider[Any]] = infer_provider) EXISTS — the epic's central seam is real; (2) BedrockConverseModel + BedrockModelSettings + BedrockModelProfile all exist under pydantic-ai-slim[bedrock]; (3) BedrockConverseModel.__init__ accepts profile: ModelProfileSpec|None — that IS the caller-supplied ModelProfile override injection path T1 doubted; (4) BedrockModelSettings carries bedrock_cache_instructions/bedrock_cache_tool_definitions/bedrock_cache_messages, so caching parity holds (direct-Anthropic has the first two only); (5) T8 answer — the differing flags are BedrockModelProfile.bedrock_supports_prompt_caching / bedrock_supports_tool_caching, and S2's output-mode read is ModelProfile.supports_json_schema_output / supports_json_object_output / default_structured_output_mode. BLOCKING G6 ANSWER: Bedrock cannot use the httpx AsyncTenacityTransport (boto3/botocore, not httpx); equivalent fidelity comes from botocore Config(retries={max_attempts, mode:adaptive}) on BedrockProvider(bedrock_client=...) plus aws_read_timeout/aws_connect_timeout. Remediating the epic description now."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785341620835347001,"uuid":"78bff55f-0bb4-4ee2-8842-40907aafc6af"}